
== u = A·U (U = 3(−sin y, sin x, 0) + (−sin x cos z, 0, cos x sin z)) ==
  max |ω| at A=1: 6;  K = 0.5 max|ω| = 3;  #high points = 18856 / 46656
  pairs used: 20000; min |x-y| among them: 0.174533
  max |sin θ| / |x-y|^(1/2) = 0.76143113
  max |sin θ| / |x-y|         = 0.61527499
  max |ξ(x)-ξ(y)| / |x-y|^(1/2) = 1.4823284
  worst Hölder pair: |ξ(x)-ξ(y)|/|x-y|^(1/2)=1.4823284, |x-y|=1.7277878, |sin θ|=0.43952198, |ξ(x)-ξ(y)|=1.9484516
  These are finite because the snapshot is C^∞ and K>0 keeps |ω| away from 0,
  so ξ is C^∞ on the high set. This is not a uniform-in-time bound for every solution.

